fixture dash_on_cling_frame_goes_away
doc docs/adr/0010, Dash "a dash ... from a wall ... goes away from it" (movement review 4, M5): after a kick, the dash pressed with the stick toward the wall on the tick the apex re-grip begins (a cling that restores nothing). A press on that tick is a press on the wall, so the dash goes away from it, as it would a tick later from the cling. (It used to be an air dash into the wall that moved nowhere, clung and spent the air dash.)
room test/shaft
spawn 760 300
frames 60
input
  0..5 R
  6..9 R
  10 R jump
  11..32 R
  33 R dash
  34..59 R
end
expect
  at 6 event.wall_cling=1
  at 10 event.wall_kick=1
  at 32 state=air air_dashes=1
  # The kick's apex cling (a re-grip, restoring nothing) begins on frame 33, the dash pressed with it.
  at 33 event.dash=1
  # Away from the wall, and the air dash spent on a real dash.
  at 34 x<x@33
  at 38 x<=-60u+x@33
end
